<main id="main">
<section class="phero"><div class="phero-bg"><img src="/assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp" srcset="/assets/img/photos/paperwork-640.webp 640w, /assets/img/photos/paperwork.webp 1200w" sizes="100vw" width="1200" height="797" alt="" fetchpriority="high" decoding="async" data-parallax="0.12"></div><div class="wrap phero-in"><nav class="crumbs" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/">Home</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><a href="/resource-center/">Resources</a><i aria-hidden="true">›</i><span aria-current="page">Glossary</span></nav><p class="tag">Reference</p><h1>Property Insurance Claim Glossary</h1><p class="lede">40 terms you’ll see in New Jersey policies, estimates and appraisal awards, defined in plain English. Type to filter.</p></div></section><div class="wrap two-col"><article class="prose"><div class="gfilter"><label for="gloss-filter">Search the glossary</label><input id="gloss-filter" type="search" placeholder="Try “holdback” or “umpire”" autocomplete="off"><p class="hint" data-gcount></p></div><div class="az"><a href="#g-A">A</a><a href="#g-C">C</a><a href="#g-D">D</a><a href="#g-E">E</a><a href="#g-F">F</a><a href="#g-H">H</a><a href="#g-I">I</a><a href="#g-L">L</a><a href="#g-M">M</a><a href="#g-N">N</a><a href="#g-O">O</a><a href="#g-P">P</a><a href="#g-R">R</a><a href="#g-S">S</a><a href="#g-U">U</a><a href="#g-W">W</a><a href="#g-X">X</a></div><dl class="glossary"><div class="gterm" id="g-A"><dt>Actual cash value (ACV)</dt><dd>Replacement cost minus depreciation. Many policies pay ACV first and the rest after repairs.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Additional living expense (ALE)</dt><dd>Coverage for extra costs of living elsewhere while your home is being repaired.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Amount of loss</dt><dd>The dollar value of covered damage. It’s the question an appraisal panel decides.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal award</dt><dd>The written decision that sets the amount of loss, binding when signed by any two of the three panel members.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraisal clause</dt><dd>The policy provision that lets either side demand appraisal when they disagree on the amount of loss.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Appraiser</dt><dd>The person each side names to value the loss. Policies usually require a competent and disinterested appraiser.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-C"><dt>Coverage A</dt><dd>Dwelling coverage for the house itself and attached structures.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage B</dt><dd>Other-structures coverage for detached garages, sheds and fences.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage C</dt><dd>Personal property coverage for contents.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Coverage D</dt><dd>Loss-of-use coverage, including additional living expenses.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-D"><dt>Debris removal</dt><dd>Coverage for removing debris after a covered loss, often with separate limits for trees.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Declarations page</dt><dd>The summary page of your policy listing limits, deductibles and endorsements.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Deductible</dt><dd>The part of a covered loss you pay before the policy pays.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Depreciation</dt><dd>The reduction in value for age and wear. Recoverable depreciation is paid after repairs under a replacement cost policy.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>DOBI</dt><dd>The New Jersey Department of Banking and Insurance, the state’s insurance regulator.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-E"><dt>Endorsement</dt><dd>A policy amendment that adds, removes or changes coverage.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-F"><dt>FAIR Plan</dt><dd>A state-backed insurer of last resort. In New Jersey it’s the New Jersey Insurance Underwriting Association.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Flood exclusion</dt><dd>The homeowners policy provision that excludes surface water, storm surge and related flooding.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-H"><dt>Holdback</dt><dd>Recoverable depreciation the insurer holds until repairs are completed.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Hurricane deductible</dt><dd>A separate deductible, often a percentage of Coverage A, that applies when the policy’s hurricane trigger is met.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-I"><dt>Ice dam</dt><dd>A ridge of ice at the eaves that traps meltwater, which can back up under shingles into the home.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-L"><dt>Line item</dt><dd>A single priced entry in an estimate, such as one square of shingles.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-M"><dt>Matching</dt><dd>Whether repaired areas must reasonably match undamaged areas in color, texture and style.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Mitigation</dt><dd>Steps taken to prevent further damage after a loss, such as tarping or drying.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-N"><dt>NFIP</dt><dd>The National Flood Insurance Program, the federal program that writes most flood insurance.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Nor’easter</dt><dd>A coastal storm with northeast winds, common in New Jersey in fall and winter.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-O"><dt>Ordinance or law coverage</dt><dd>Coverage for added costs of meeting building codes during repairs.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Overhead and profit (O&amp;P)</dt><dd>A general contractor’s charge for coordinating a repair, often 10% plus 10%.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-P"><dt>Proof of loss</dt><dd>A sworn statement of the amount claimed, sometimes required by the insurer.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Public adjuster</dt><dd>A state-licensed professional who represents policyholders in handling and negotiating claims.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-R"><dt>Replacement cost value (RCV)</dt><dd>The cost to repair or replace damaged property with similar materials, without depreciation.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Reservation of rights</dt><dd>A letter in which the insurer investigates while reserving the right to deny coverage.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-S"><dt>Scope</dt><dd>The list of damaged items and repairs included in an estimate.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Square</dt><dd>100 square feet of roof surface.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Suit limitation</dt><dd>The policy deadline for filing a lawsuit against the insurer, often 12 months in New Jersey.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Supplement</dt><dd>A request to add items or costs to an existing estimate.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-U"><dt>Umpire</dt><dd>The neutral third panel member who decides items the appraisers can’t agree on.</dd></div><div class="gterm"><dt>Uniform Construction Code (UCC)</dt><dd>New Jersey’s statewide building code, which governs permits and repairs.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-W"><dt>Windstorm deductible</dt><dd>A deductible that applies to wind losses generally, broader than a hurricane deductible.</dd></div><div class="gterm" id="g-X"><dt>Xactimate</dt><dd>Estimating software widely used by insurers and contractors to price repairs.</dd></div></dl><p class="gnone" hidden>No terms match that search.</p></article><aside class="aside"><div class="aside-in"><div class="box callbox"><h2 class="box-t">Talk through your claim</h2><p>The first conversation is free. We’ll tell you honestly whether appraisal fits.</p><a class="callbox-num" href="tel:+18445371427"><svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M22 16.9v3a2 2 0 0 1-2.2 2 19.8 19.8 0 0 1-8.6-3.1 19.5 19.5 0 0 1-6-6A19.8 19.8 0 0 1 2.1 4.2 2 2 0 0 1 4.1 2h3a2 2 0 0 1 2 1.7c.1.9.4 1.8.7 2.7a2 2 0 0 1-.5 2.1L8 9.8a16 16 0 0 0 6 6l1.3-1.3a2 2 0 0 1 2.1-.4c.9.3 1.8.6 2.7.7a2 2 0 0 1 1.7 2z"/></svg> (844) 537-1427</a><a class="btn ink" href="/contact-us/">Send claim details</a></div><div class="box"><h2 class="box-t">Resource center</h2><ul class="box-list"><li><a href="/resource-center/appraisal-process/">Appraisal process guide<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/resource-center/faq/">Appraisal FAQ<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/resource-center/glossary/" aria-current="page">Claim glossary<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li><li><a href="/resource-center/articles/">Articles<svg width="20" height="20" viewBox="0 0 24 24" fill="none" stroke="currentColor" stroke-width="2" stroke-linecap="round" stroke-linejoin="round" aria-hidden="true" focusable="false"><path d="M5 12h14M13 6l6 6-6 6"/></svg></a></li></ul></div></div></aside></div>
